  "solution": "**Given:-**\n\nx+ y =√13 \n\nx - y =√11\n\n**Formula used:-**\n\n(x+ y )² - (x - y)² = 4xy \n\n \n\n(x+ y )2 + (x - y)2 = 2( x²+ y²)\n\n**Calculation:-**\n\n (x+ y)2 + (x - y)2 = 2( x2+ y2)\n\n⇒ 2( x2+ y2) = (√13 )² + (√11)² \n\n⇒ 2( x2+ y2) = 13 + 11 = 24 \n\n⇒ ( x2+ y2) = 12 .....(1)\n\n (x+ y)2 - (x - y)2 = 4xy \n\n⇒ 4xy = (√13 )2 - (√11)2 \n\n⇒ 4xy = 2 \n\n⇒ xy =1/2....(2)\n\nMultiplying (1) & (2) \n\n⇒ xy ( x2+ y2) = 12 × (1/2) \n\n⇒ xy ( x2+ y2) = 6 \n\n**∴ The required answer is 6.**",
